-- title:
--   Twisted elliptic-central fold equals base-changed central-elliptic kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields whose degree $[L:K]$ is prime, let $0<\alpha<\beta$, and let $\Phi_L$ be a subset of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ contained in the slab where the idele norm of the determinant lies in $[\alpha,\beta]$ and a fundamental domain for the image of $GL_2(L)$ acting on that slab with the restricted adelic Haar measure; let $\nu_{Z,L}$ be a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ with fundamental domain $\Omega_L$ for the image of $L^\times$, and let $\Phi_K,\nu_{Z,K},\Omega_K$ be the analogous data over $K$. Further data: a datum $D$ giving a continuous action of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ on $\mathbb{A}_L$ compatible with the embedding of $L$; an element $\sigma\neq 1$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$; a finite set $S_K$ of finite places of $K$ outside which all places of $L$ have ramification index $1$; a character $\xi_L$ of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$, continuous and trivial on principal ideles; the finite set $\Xi$ consisting exactly of those characters $\xi_K$ of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ that are continuous, trivial on $K^\times$ and satisfy $\xi_K\circ N = \xi_L$ for the idelic norm of the base-change datum [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87). Two hypotheses are assumed: (i) every $\gamma\in GL_2(K)$ whose characteristic polynomial has no root in $K$ and which, at every finite place $v$ and over the infinite adeles, is a norm in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L217) for $\sigma^{-1}$ (conjugate to a $\sigma^{-1}$-norm string of some element of $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, resp. $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_\infty)$), has conjugacy class in the range of [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766); (ii) for every Haar measure $\mu_L$ on $GL_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$ there is a nonzero $c_0\in\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ such that, for every finite $S'\supseteq S_K$, any pair $(\varphi,f)$ matching at $S'$ in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingAt`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L557) and whose unramified local data (indicators of the semilocal and local integral sets) match at the places outside $S'$ has, after transport of $\varphi$ along the ring isomorphism $L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K\cong\mathbb{A}_K\otimes_K L\cong\mathbb{A}_L$, matching adelic orbital integrals for $\mu_L$ and $c_0\cdot$(adelic Haar measure). The conclusion: there exists $c\in\mathbb{C}$, $c\neq 0$, such that for every finite $S'\supseteq S_K$ and every continuous compactly supported $\varphi$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $f$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ matching at $S'$ and satisfying the same unramified local matching condition, the integral over $x\in\Phi_L$ and $z\in\Omega_L$ of $\xi_L(z)$ times the (finite-support) sum over those $\delta\in GL_2(L)$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class has norm class equal to the class of some $\gamma\in GL_2(K)$ that is either scalar or has no eigenvalue in $K$, of $\varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(z x)\bigr)$, equals $c$ times $\sum_{\xi_K\in\Xi}$ of the integral over $x\in\Phi_K$, $z\in\Omega_K$ of $\xi_K(z)$ times the sum of the central and elliptic parts of the adelic kernel of $f$ at $(x,zx)$, i.e. $\sum_{\gamma}f(x^{-1}\gamma z x)$ over scalar $\gamma$ and over $\gamma$ with no eigenvalue in $K$.
--
--   This is the first row of Langlands's comparison, for a cyclic extension of prime degree, of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $GL(2)$ over $L$ with the trace formula over $K$: the $\sigma$-elliptic and central-norm contributions on the twisted side are identified with the elliptic and central contributions on the base side, up to one global constant and summation over the characters of $K$ lifting $\xi_L$. Two classical inputs are carried as hypotheses here — the norm principle for elliptic classes and the passage from local matching to matching of the global orbital integrals — and the result is used by the version of the comparison in which those hypotheses are discharged.
